      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent nanoprecipitates relieve local stress concentrations that can otherwise cause premature crack initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoprecipitates provide nucleation sites for dislocation movement.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoprecipitate-mediated stress redistribution delays crack initiation in WTaTiVZr relative to pure tungsten.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pure tungsten lacks the proposed nanoprecipitate-mediated deformation mechanism.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pure tungsten has lower plastic strain and toughness than WTaTiVZr under similar high-temperature loading.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under high-temperature loading, WTaTiVZr will exhibit greater plastic strain and toughness than pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "WTaTiVZr will show delayed crack propagation relative to pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical loading at 800–1100 °C is relevant to sustained plasma-facing-component service.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::page::001",
        "PMC10813983::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoprecipitates remain structurally stable throughout approximately 800–1100 °C.",
